      "body": "**Why.** `tools/check_process_group_usage.py` is report-only on main (#7986), so drift in its allowlist does not fail CI. On main it now reports 3 new reads and misses 1 stale entry. Every pull request that runs the check gets the same 3 lines in its log, whether or not it touches those files.\n- #7394 added a second `get_tensor_and_data_parallel_group()` read in `finalize_model_grads`.\n- #7156 added a `use_mpu_process_groups()` fallback in `SimplifiedDSGQAIndexer.__init__`.\n- #4743 added a `get_expert_tensor_and_model_parallel_group()` fallback in `DynamicInferenceContext.__init__`.\n- #7047 removed the `use_mpu_process_groups()` call in `_CudaGraphRunner._set_gtp_finalize_hook_plan`, so its entry is stale.\n\n**What.**\n- Record the three reads in `tools/process_group_usage_allowlist.json` and drop the stale entry. The total goes from 194 to 196.\n- No code changes. The reads stay where they are; the slices of #6307 that own those files remove them.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `python tools/check_process_group_usage.py`: \"OK: no new global process-group reads (196 grandfathered)\". On main it lists the 3 reads.\n- `python tests/unit_tests/test_check_process_group_usage.py`: 29 tests pass.\n\nPart of #6307.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
